{"result":"{
  "id": "18356",
  "key": "SFCC-194",
  "summary": "PDP – Was/Now Sale Price",
  "url": "https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/rest/api/2/issue/18356",
  "description": "**As a** Shopper,\n\n**I want** to see both the original and sale price clearly displayed on the PDP when a product is on sale,\n\n**so that** I can understand the discount before deciding to buy.\n\n----\n\nImage for reference (Figma is leading):\n\n![\"image-20260814-042632.png\"](image-20260814-042632.png)\n\n\n\nWhen a product has an active sale price in SFCC (driven by a sale pricebook), the PDP displays both the original price (Was) and the sale price (Now). The sale price takes visual prominence. When no sale price is active, only the standard price is displayed. Price display is consistent across all storefronts with appropriate currency formatting per region.\n\nThis story covers the PDP price display only. Pricebook configuration and sale pricebook management are out of scope.",
  "status": {
    "name": "In Progress",
    "category": "In Progress",
    "color": "yellow"
  },
  "issue_type": {
    "name": "Story"
  },
  "priority": {
    "name": "High"
  },
  "assignee": {
